<newsitem itemid="226147" id="root" date="1996-11-29" xml:lang="en">
<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore Telecom 1st-half net rises.</title>
<headline>Singapore Telecom 1st-half net rises.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>(millions of Singapore dollars unless specified)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   843.5  vs 742.5</p>
<p>    Group earnings per share (cts)   5.53 vs   4.87</p>
<p>    Turnover (billions)		  2.17 vs   1.96</p>
<p>    Operating profit(blns)	     1.09 vs   0.97</p>
<p>    Associates	  (profit)	 1.1  vs   31.1 (loss)</p>
<p>    Interest income		     49.4  vs   32.8</p>
<p>    Investment income		   24.6  vs   19.3</p>
<p>    Interest expense		    15.2  vs   20.4</p>
<p>    Other income		 (loss) 11.5  vs   17.9 (gain)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit (blns)		1.13 vs   0.99</p>
<p>    Tax				    290.4  vs  243.1</p>
<p>    Minorities		 (loss)    0.50 vs    0.60 (profit)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	 (profit) 148.4  vs    nil</p>
<p>Note -- Singapore Press Holdings said the extraordinary gain came from profit on sale of long term investments.</p>
</text>
